---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="FAQ - usignpdf"
  seo={{
    page_description: "Answers to common questions about e-signatures, legality, and using usignpdf.",
    canonical_url: "https://usignpdf.com/faq/"
  }}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 px-4 md:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-12 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Are electronic signatures legally binding?</h3>
        <p class="text-text-muted">Yes. Under the <a href="/legality/us-esign-act" class="underline">ESIGN Act</a> (US), <a href="/legality/eu-eidas" class="underline">eIDAS</a> (EU), and equivalent laws globally, electronic signatures are legally binding and enforceable in court, provided they meet certain criteria which usignpdf fulfills. Learn more in our <a href="/legality" class="underline">Legality reference</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Do my clients need to create an account?</h3>
        <p class="text-text-muted">Never. Your clients simply click the link you send them, sign the document, and download their copy. We believe in zero friction for signers.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">What is an Audit Trail?</h3>
        <p class="text-text-muted">An <a href="/security/audit-trails" class="underline">audit trail</a> is a digital record that logs the steps of the signing process. Ours includes the signer's IP address, timestamp, and a cryptographic hash of the document to prove it hasn't been altered.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Is my data secure?</h3>
        <p class="text-text-muted">Yes. Documents are <a href="/security/encryption" class="underline">encrypted</a> at rest and in transit using bank-level AES-256 encryption. We never share your data with third parties. Read about our <a href="/compliance" class="underline">compliance</a> standards.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
